    "code_released": "not stated",
    "peer_reviewed": "preprint",
    "problems": "The result is scoped to temperature zero, vLLM v0.19, Llama and Qwen families, the tested acceptance methods, and the listed safety battery; sampling temperatures, other frameworks, and tree-speculation variants are untested. The paper reports per-cell MDE of 7.4–8.3pp and pooled MDE of approximately 4.3pp. The h cutoff was calibrated post hoc on expansion data, though the paper reports a held-out calibration check. Expansion-cell conclusions use deterministic classifiers rather than the core LLM-judge pipeline.",
    "rows_left_out": "No separate rows for byte-identity, capability-task results, or safety tasks other than AdvBench refusal: these do not directly measure the harmful-request refusal outcome named by V4. The one-arm E1 70B speculative-only refusal rate is not a matched decoding-change comparison and is not included as a V4 result.",
